# Revisions to skip when running `git blame` — bulk mechanical rewrites
# that would otherwise attribute every touched line to a reformat.
#
# Enable it once per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# (GitHub honours this file automatically in its blame view.)
#
# Only add commits that changed formatting and nothing else. A commit
# listed here still shows up in `git log`; blame just looks through it to
# the revision that last changed the line's substance.
#
# CAVEAT for the cresset monorepo: these are the **monorepo's** commit ids.
# The canonical tree lives at ~/cresset, whose history was rewritten
# beneath each project path on import, so the same change carries a
# different id in `cresset-tools/bougie`. `git blame` fails hard on a rev
# it cannot resolve, so if this file is ever synced downstream the entries
# must be translated to that repo's ids — not copied verbatim. Likewise, a
# rebase of an unpushed entry changes its id; re-record it if that happens.

